Nepa Keyboard internal Yakkha layout notice

The Yakkha phone layout is an Ampixa-authored adaptation of the reviewed
Nepali phone layout derived from xkeyboard-config's Nepal symbols file in
xkb-data 2.41-2ubuntu1.1.

The complete upstream aggregate copyright and license text is included in the
same internal keyboard artifact as:

    xkb-data-2.41-2ubuntu1.1.copyright

Its pinned SHA-256 is:

    739ff5404b852466ed201799e49bb5dc0f4eafe0876bf9aa74499f306b7b1786

Upstream source:
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xkeyboard-config/xkeyboard-config/-/blob/xkeyboard-config-2.41/symbols/np

Upstream license:
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xkeyboard-config/xkeyboard-config/-/blob/xkeyboard-config-2.41/COPYING

The Yakkha-specific five-key language row, terminal-ZWNJ input semantics, and
symbols-layer backslash placement are project-authored internal additions.
